+  // 1. the page's in-memory copy guard listens for "copy" on window and
+  //    stores the clipboard text as its "last copied" value; dispatching a
+  //    synthetic copy event carrying the text makes that guard accept any
+  //    later paste of the same text unchanged. Dispatching on window itself
+  //    keeps the event away from the page's document-level copy blockers.
+  // 2. older builds of such pages keep that record in localStorage under a
+  //    letter-shift cipher; writing it too keeps those builds working.
